        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: કપાવું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "કપાવું — kapāvũ — \"to get cut\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "છરીથી મારી આંગળી કપાઈ ગઈ. charīthī mārī ā̃gaḷī kapāī gaī. I cut my finger on the knife."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): તે આંગળી કપાઈ ગઈ, te ā̃gaḷī kapāī gaī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "કપાવું (kapāvũ) is the intransitive partner of કાપવું (kāpvũ), \"to cut\", which goes back to Sanskrit kalpayati, \"trims, cuts\" (CDIAL 2944)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
